  "scope": "Native original-account retirement inventory, report, independent host acknowledgement and logical journal/signer erasure. Managed-controller and installed foreign integration remain open.",
  "behavior": [
    "Only a verified permanent account retirement selects an original frozen subject; the actual domain-separated root proposal binding is retained.",
    "Witness lookup uses the original subject account; previously retained device inventories cannot be overwritten by a later account-root inventory.",
    "The original enrollment lease transfers into the existing restricted cleanup owner. Root history and original enrollment bytes remain alongside the exact cleanup inventory.",
    "The journal image, pending intent and exact root fence are erased in one transaction only after purpose-21 host acknowledgement. The original signer is prepared and erased separately afterwards.",
    "Actual unconfirmed ciphertext identities survive reporting. Prepared and committed pending targets remain distinct. No delivery success, successor authority or physical erasure is inferred."
  ],
